From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 01 Jul 2026 14:44:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: bind wifi NPU egress flows in PPE

Downstream (PON->WiFi) flows never bind in the PPE. The tx_modified
gate in airoha_ppe_foe_insert_entry() defers the FOE commit until
the egress TX path populates the egress-side fields which was not
happening.

For mt76 NPU offload the egress description (WDMA band, WCID, BSS,
PSE port CDM4) is fully known at rule-replace time from
dev_fill_forward_path(), so mark wifi-egress entries tx_modified
when they are created in airoha_set_flow_destination().

Also fix two issues hidden behind the missing bind:

- arht_modified_ppe_entry() detects wifi netdevs by MTK driver
  names (phy0/ra*/apcli*/ap-mld*). OpenWrt wlan netdevs fell
  through to the GDM branch, failed validation and returned early
  without writing the L2 MAC rewrite fields. Detect wifi from the
  prepared FOE entry (PSE port CDM4) instead.

- Set IB2 DSCP for wifi egress in airoha_ppe_foe_entry_prepare()
  so the NPU can map flows to the proper WMM queue, matching what
  the unused vendor wifi TX hook would have programmed.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c |    6 +++
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_ppe.c   |   35 +++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 37 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -369,9 +369,13 @@ static int airoha_ppe_foe_entry_prepare(
 
 		if (!airoha_ppe_get_wdma_info(netdev, data->eth.h_dest,
 					      &info)) {
+			/* NPU expects the 6-bit DSCP for CDM4 egress, unlike
+			 * the GDM path which stores the full TOS byte.
+			 */
 			val |= FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB2_NBQ, info.idx) |
 			       FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB2_PSE_PORT,
-					  FE_PSE_PORT_CDM4);
+					  FE_PSE_PORT_CDM4) |
+			       FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB2_DSCP, dsfield >> 2);
 			qdata |= FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_ACTDP, info.bss);
 			wlan_etype = FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_MAC_WDMA_BAND,
 						info.idx) |
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_ppe.c
@@ -3589,6 +3589,26 @@ int __airoha_ppe_foe_commit_entry(struct
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/* Detect wifi egress from the prepared FOE entry itself: the wdma branch of
+ * airoha_ppe_foe_entry_prepare() selects FE_PSE_PORT_CDM4. Name-based checks
+ * (airoha_ppe_is_wifi_dev) only match the MTK proprietary driver, and the
+ * flow rule may carry the bridge netdev rather than the wlan vif.
+ */
+static bool arht_foe_entry_is_wifi(struct airoha_foe_entry *hwe)
+{
+	int type = FIELD_GET(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_PACKET_TYPE, hwe->ib1);
+	u32 ib2;
+
+	if (type == PPE_PKT_TYPE_BRIDGE)
+		ib2 = hwe->bridge.ib2;
+	else if (type >= PPE_PKT_TYPE_IPV6_ROUTE_3T)
+		ib2 = hwe->ipv6.ib2;
+	else
+		ib2 = hwe->ipv4.ib2;
+
+	return FIELD_GET(AIROHA_FOE_IB2_PSE_PORT, ib2) == FE_PSE_PORT_CDM4;
+}
+
 void airoha_set_flow_destination(struct net_device *dev, struct airoha_flow_table_entry *e)
 {
         if(!dev || !e){
@@ -3600,13 +3620,22 @@ void airoha_set_flow_destination(struct
                 AIROHA_LOG(AIROHA_DEBUG_LEVEL_ERR, "destination set to PON\n");
                 e->e_magic = PON;
         }
-		
+
 		if(airoha_get_lan_id(dev))
 		{
 			AIROHA_LOG(AIROHA_DEBUG_LEVEL_ERR, "destination set to ETH\n");
             e->e_magic = airoha_get_lan_id(dev);
 		}
 
+        if(arht_foe_entry_is_wifi(&e->data)){
+                AIROHA_LOG(AIROHA_DEBUG_LEVEL_ERR, "destination set to WIFI\n");
+                /* mt76 NPU egress is fully described at rule-replace time via
+                 * dev_fill_forward_path(); no QDMA TX pass ever runs for wifi
+                 * to set tx_modified, so grant commit-eligibility here.
+                 */
+                e->tx_modified = true;
+        }
+
         return;
 }
 
@@ -3944,9 +3973,9 @@ void arht_modified_ppe_entry(struct airo
 		return;
 	}
 
-	if (airoha_ppe_is_wifi_dev(netdev)) {
+	if (airoha_ppe_is_wifi_dev(netdev) || arht_foe_entry_is_wifi(hwe)) {
 	    airoha_set_ppe_mac(hwe, netdev, data->eth.h_source, data->eth.h_dest, data->pppoe.sid);
-	    return; 
+	    return;
 	}
 
 	struct airoha_gdm_dev *dev = airoha_ppe_get_gdm_dev(glb_eth, netdev);
